    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d399">

                <pb facs="0699" n="665" sameAs="frus:frus1948v02/pg665"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Germany)/11–2648</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Permanent Under-Secretary of State for the
                        German Section</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Strang</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Douglas</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d399-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">[<hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-11-26">November 26, 1948</date>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>You will recall that during the meeting between Mr. Marshall, M. Schuman and
                    Mr. McNeil in Paris on 19 November<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d399-f2"/> the Minister of State made the suggestion that you,
                        M. Massigli, and I should call for a
                    progress report from the Military Governors on their discussions relating to the
                    establishment of the Military Security Board for Germany, for which provision is
                    made in Annex L of the report on the London talks on Germany dated 1 June
                        1948.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d399-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>The British Military Governor in Germany has been informed accordingly and,
                    unless they see objections, the US Government may <pb facs="0700" n="666"
                        xml:id="pg666"/> wish to arrange that instructions be sent to the US
                    Military Governor requesting him to associate himself with General Robertson in the preparation of a joint report
                    on the discussions on the Military Security Board, following the meeting of the
                    Military Governors on 30 November.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d399-f4"/>
                </p>
                <p>I am writing in similar terms to the French Ambassador.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d399-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d399-f1-content">
                <p>The source text was transmitted to Ambassador Douglas, who was visiting briefly in Paris, in telegram 934,
                    November 26, from the Chargé in London to Paris, repeated to the Department of
                    State as telegram 5015.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d399-f2" n="2" xml:id="d399-f2-content">
                <p>For the minutes of the meeting under reference here, see <ref target="#pg517">p.
                        517</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d399-f3" n="3" xml:id="d399-f3-content">
                <p>Regarding the documents under reference here, see the editorial note, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d399-f4" n="4" xml:id="d399-f4-content">
                <p>Telegram 6077, November 29, from Paris, not printed, reported that the French
                    Government had instructed General Koenig
                    to make a request at the next meeting of the American, British and French
                    Military Governors for a prompt report from the working party on security
                    (740.00119 Control (Germany)/11–2948). Telegram 1880, November 29, to Berlin,
                    not printed, stated that the Department of the Army was requesting General
                        Clay to associate himself with the
                    other Military Governors in the preparation of a report by the working party on
                    security (740.00119 Control (Germany)/11–2948).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
